github.com/belluikit/goffmpeg-libs/windows_arm64
================================================

shared/ contains FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org) built for windows_arm64 as shared
libraries, so that an app ships them and a user can replace them (LGPL 2.1
section 6b):

  avcodec-goffmpeg-63.dll avdevice-goffmpeg-63.dll avformat-goffmpeg-63.dll avutil-goffmpeg-61.dll libavcodec-goffmpeg.dll.a libavdevice-goffmpeg.dll.a libavformat-goffmpeg.dll.a libavutil-goffmpeg.dll.a libswresample-goffmpeg.dll.a libswscale-goffmpeg.dll.a swresample-goffmpeg-7.dll swscale-goffmpeg-10.dll

lib/ contains libgoffmpeg.dll, goffmpeg's purego bridge (see Bridge below).

FFmpeg version: N-125841-ge2bc6d88cd (git revision e2bc6d88cd68184288c16570e04881c3a426a05a).
No local patches: goffmpeg's build applies patches/*.patch to the FFmpeg
checkout, and goffmpeg has no such files (BUILDING.md: "The directory is
currently empty").

License: GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later. The full
text is in LICENSE at the root of this repository, and is included in this
module's zip by the go command. The build used neither --enable-gpl nor
--enable-nonfree; each library reports "license: LGPL version 2.1 or later".

lib/libgoffmpeg.dll and the DLLs in shared/ are linked by llvm-mingw 20261006 and so
contain parts of the MinGW-w64 runtime (startup code and C runtime glue).
Some of it requires its copyright and license notices to accompany
binaries: they are in COPYING.MinGW-w64-runtime.txt in this module, taken
from mingw-w64's own copy of that file. The static libraries in lib/
contain no runtime code.
llvm-mingw's compiler-rt builtins are linked too, under Apache-2.0 WITH
LLVM-exception, which does not require a notice for compiled code.

Configure line of shared/, as recorded in its libavutil (avutil_configuration()).

  --prefix=/windows_arm64 --extra-cflags=-fPIC --enable-pic --disable-autodetect --disable-programs --disable-doc --disable-debug --disable-encoders --disable-muxers --disable-avfilter --enable-swscale --enable-swresample --enable-network --arch=aarch64 --target-os=mingw32 --enable-cross-compile --cross-prefix=/opt/llvm-mingw/bin/aarch64-w64-mingw32- --enable-schannel --enable-avdevice --enable-indev=dshow --enable-shared --disable-static --build-suffix=-goffmpeg

Corresponding source:
  FFmpeg:  https://github.com/belluikit/ffmpeg/tree/goffmpeg-e2bc6d88cd
           belluikit's mirror of FFmpeg. The tag is commit
           e2bc6d88cd68184288c16570e04881c3a426a05a and stays for as long as
           libraries built from it are published.
  Build:   https://github.com/belluikit/goffmpeg (Makefile, BUILDING.md), which
           pins that revision and this configure line.
  Bridge:  lib/libgoffmpeg.* is goffmpeg's bridge.c (BSD-3-Clause), built by
           goffmpeg's 'make bridge-shared'. It holds no FFmpeg code: it loads
           the DLLs in shared/, which must be beside the executable or on PATH.
           The current lib/libgoffmpeg.* was built from goffmpeg commit
           56ff0d7 by GitHub Actions run 42614744092.
  Shared:  shared/ was built by goffmpeg's 'make dist-shared' (now 'make
           dist') from goffmpeg commit 2eb34b5 by GitHub Actions run
           42569150705.
